Source for LIMSOC Permission Assist. The host serves the built copy in `site/` to signed-in members.

- `src/page.html`, `src/app.js`: the page. Edit these.
- `data/`: the staging snapshot (example view and permission labels), the baseline permission list, and the group column order.
- `vendor/xlsx.full.min.js`: SheetJS 0.18.5, hash-pinned in `build.py`.
- `build.py`: writes `site/index.html`, `site/vendor/xlsx.full.min.js` and the file hashes in `poc.json`.
- `make-test-csv.ts`: writes `test/groups-export-test.csv`, a Groups export made from the staging snapshot, for checking upload and download.

## Changing the page

```
python3 page/build.py
bun page/make-test-csv.ts      # only if the group names or the snapshot changed
git add -A && git commit
```

Never edit `site/` by hand. `bun test` fails if `site/` or `poc.json` differ from a fresh build, and a push to `main` deploys.

## Group names the page treats specially

- **Superuser**: holds every permission after "Choose all".
- **Superuser (Do not update manually)**: the reference group. It records what Superuser held at the previous run; new permissions are the ones in Superuser that are not in it. The import file sets both groups to the full list. Matching ignores case. (Until 23 Nov 2026 this group was called "Superuser (last run)". No group of that name was ever imported into LIMSOC, so the old name is not recognised.)

The page never calls LIMSOC. Import testing is done by hand on staging.limsoc.com.au only.
''')
