cd /home/nicholas-wood/.claude/jobs/64af022a/tmp/pp
python3 - <<'EOF'
import pathlib,json
m=json.loads(pathlib.Path('poc.json').read_text())
for c in m['capabilities']:
    if c['name']=='storage': c['usage']="Per member: the member's work (last export uploaded, ticks, added groups, Include choices, open group, group rules) so it opens the same in any browser. Shared: one record (key lsvperm-seen) of the last export uploaded and the last import file downloaded, so a group edited by hand in LIMSOC is called out for every member."
    if c['name']=='user': c['usage']="The member's email: shown beside the shared record, and used to clear a browser's saved copy when a different member signs in on it."
pathlib.Path('poc.json').write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2)+'\n')
p=pathlib.Path('page/README.md'); s=p.read_text()
a=s.index('## Keeping your work'); b=s.index('## Adding groups')
s=s[:a]+'''## Keeping your work

A refresh, another browser or another computer opens the page where you left it: the last export you uploaded, with its ticks, added groups, step 4 Include choices, the group open in step 3 and the note about changes in LIMSOC from when it was uploaded, plus your group rules. The staging example only shows if you have never uploaded anything. Uploading a new export replaces it. The top bar says "Saved to your account", "Saving…", or that saving failed and is being retried.

How: on the LSV POC host your work is kept against your account in this POC's database, through the host's per-member storage (`window.claude.storage`, keys `lsvperm.*`, not shared). The browser keeps a working copy in localStorage so the page stays instant; every change is copied up as it happens, and the page reads your saved work back when it opens and when you upload an export it has seen before. If you try to leave while a change is still saving, the browser asks first. If a different member signs in on the same browser, the copy the last member left there is cleared before theirs is read. Work kept in a browser before accounts were used moves up to the account the first time it opens.

Opened as a local file (no host), the same work is kept in that browser only.

Each change replaces the saved copy, so two browsers editing at the same moment end with whichever saved last. Only the five most recent exports keep their saved work, and the last export is about 120 KB, well inside the host's 500 KB per item. Reopening never writes to the shared change record; only an upload or a download does.

'''+s[b:]
p.write_text(s)
EOF
cat >> test/page.test.ts <<'EOF'

describe("work kept against the member's account", () => {
  const app = readFileSync("page/src/app.js", "utf8");
  test("every save goes through the account copy", () => {
    expect(app).not.toMatch(/localStorage\.setItem\((?!SKEY|lk,|OKEY)/);
    expect(app).toContain("function lsSet(k,v)");
    expect(app).toContain("window.claude.storage.set(k,v)");
  });
  test("saved work is per member, never shared", () => {
    expect(app).not.toMatch(/storage\.(set|get)\(k,[^)]*shared/);
    expect(app).toContain("return 'lsvperm.f.'+fnv(rest)+'.'+suf;");
  });
  test("the page reads the account copy before it opens and before an upload", () => {
    expect(app).toContain("pullAll().then(boot,");
    expect(app).toContain("if(HOSTED)pullFile(sig).then(go,go)");
  });
  test("a different member on the same browser does not see the last member's work", () => {
    expect(app).toContain("if(me&&owner&&owner!==me)ourKeys().forEach");
  });
  test("leaving while a change is still saving asks first", () => {
    expect(app).toContain("if(HOSTED&&syncBusy()){e.preventDefault()");
  });
});
EOF
python3 page/build.py >/dev/null && python3 page/build.py --check && bun run typecheck 2>&1 | tail -1 && bun test 2>&1 | rg ' pass| fail' && bun run scripts/verify-site.ts
git add -A && git -c user.name="Nicholas Wood" -c user.email="$(git log -1 --format=%ae)" commit -q -m "feat: keep each member's work on the server so it opens the same in any browser

On the LSV POC host every saved item (last export, ticks, added groups,
Include choices, open group, group rules) is copied to the member's own
storage through the bridge and read back on open and before an upload.
localStorage stays the working copy. The top bar shows the save state,
leaving mid-save asks first, a different member signing in on the same
browser clears the previous member's copy, and browser-only work moves up
to the account the first time. Local-file use is unchanged." 
git checkout -q add-groups && git merge -q --ff-only server-state && git push -q origin add-groups 2>&1 | tail -1; git log --oneline | head -3

